  ],
  "steps": [
    "0 | In a **doubly linked list** each node also has a **prev** pointer, back to the node before it. | - | Doubly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30.",
    "1 | So arrows go both ways: **next** along the top, **prev** underneath. The list keeps a **head** and a **tail**. | - | Doubly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "2 | Make a new node for **4**. Nothing points to it yet. | head-create | Doubly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30. Being linked in or out: 4.",
    "3 | Point its **next** at the current head, 12. | head-link | Doubly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30. Being linked in or out: 4.",
    "4 | And point 12’s **prev** back at the new node. | head-link-back | Doubly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30. Being linked in or out: 4.",
    "5 | Move **head** to the new node. Nothing else moved: **O(1)**. | head-move | Doubly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30.",
    "6 | Make a new node for **9**. Nothing points to it yet. | tail-create | Doubly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30. Being linked in or out: 9.",
    "7 | The **tail** pointer finds the last node, 30, at once. Point its **next** at the new node. | tail-link | Doubly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. Being linked in or out: 9.",
    "8 | And point the new node’s **prev** back at 30. | tail-link-back | Doubly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. Being linked in or out: 9.",
    "9 | Move **tail** to the new node. No walking: **O(1)** with a tail pointer. | tail-move | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9.",
    "10 | Both ends are **O(1)**: there’s a pointer to each, and only a few pointers change. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9.",
    "11 | With prev pointers you can also insert **before** a node, which a singly linked list can’t. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9.",
    "12 | Is **cur** (4) the **30** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. cur at 4.",
    "13 | Is **cur** (12) the **30** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. cur at 12.",
    "14 | Is **cur** (7) the **30** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. cur at 7.",
    "15 | **cur** holds **30**. Found it. | search-found | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. cur at 30. Found 30.",
    "16 | Make a new node for **15**. Nothing points to it yet. | before-create | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. Being linked in or out: 15.",
    "17 | Point the new node’s **next** at 30 and its **prev** at 7. | before-link | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 9. Being linked in or out: 15.",
    "18 | Now 7’s **next** and 30’s **prev** point at **15**. | before-relink | Doubly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 15, 30, 9. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "19 | A singly linked list needs the node **before** the one it deletes. Here every node knows both neighbours. | - | Doubly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 15, 30, 9.",
    "20 | Is **cur** (4) the **7** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | delete-find | Doubly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 15, 30, 9. cur at 4.",
    "21 | Is **cur** (12) the **7** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | delete-find | Doubly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 15, 30, 9. cur at 12.",
    "22 | **cur** holds **7**. This is the node to remove. | delete-find | Doubly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 15, 30, 9. cur at 7. Found 7.",
    "23 | Point 12’s **next** past **7**, to 15. | unlink-forward | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. Being linked in or out: 7.",
    "24 | Point 15’s **prev** past **7**, back to 12. The node knew both neighbours: **O(1)**. | unlink-back | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. Being linked in or out: 7.",
    "25 | Nothing points to **7** any more, so it’s gone. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9.",
    "26 | Once you have the node, unlinking it is **O(1)**: ideal when something else, like a hash table, hands you the node. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "27 | Start **cur** at the tail and follow **prev** to walk the list backwards. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9.",
    "28 | Visit **9**. | back-visit | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. cur at 9.",
    "29 | Visit **30**. | back-visit | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. cur at 30.",
    "30 | Visit **15**. | back-visit | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. cur at 15.",
    "31 | Visit **12**. | back-visit | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. cur at 12.",
    "32 | Visit **4**. | back-visit | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. cur at 4.",
    "33 | **cur** reached null: all 5 nodes visited backwards, from the tail. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "34 | The price: every node stores two pointers instead of one. More memory, and more pointers to keep right. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9.",
    "35 | Choose a doubly linked list when you need to go backwards or delete known nodes fast, like a browser’s history. | - | Doubly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 15, 30, 9. | ⏸ chapter-end",
  ],
}
