    "42 | 288 mod 5 = 3, so **Jim** belongs in bucket 3. | hash-index | Hash table, 5 buckets, 5 keys, load factor 1.00. Bucket 0: Ann. Bucket 2: Ben. Bucket 3: Sid, Jim, Kat. 288 mod 5 = 3.",
    "43 | Is **Sid** the key **Jim**? No: next in the chain. | c-remove-compare | Hash table, 5 buckets, 5 keys, load factor 1.00. Bucket 0: Ann. Bucket 2: Ben. Bucket 3: Sid, Jim, Kat.",
    "44 | Found **Jim**: 555-0110. | c-remove-compare | Hash table, 5 buckets, 5 keys, load factor 1.00. Bucket 0: Ann. Bucket 2: Ben. Bucket 3: Sid, Jim, Kat. Found Jim.",
    "45 | Unlink **Jim** from bucket 3’s chain. The rest of the chain closes up. | c-remove-unlink | Hash table, 5 buckets, 4 keys, load factor 0.80. Bucket 0: Ann. Bucket 2: Ben. Bucket 3: Sid, Kat.",
    "46 | Delete finds the key the same way, then unlinks it from its chain. | - | Hash table, 5 buckets, 4 keys, load factor 0.80. Bucket 0: Ann. Bucket 2: Ben. Bucket 3: Sid, Kat. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "47 | The **load factor** is keys ÷ buckets: here 3 ÷ 4 = 0.75. The fuller the table, the longer its chains. | - | Hash table, 4 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.75. Bucket 1: Ann, Ben. Bucket 3: Mia.",
    "48 | So a table sets a limit, often 0.75. A put that would go over it makes the table bigger first. | - | Hash table, 4 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.75. Bucket 1: Ann, Ben. Bucket 3: Mia.",
    "49 | 4 keys in 4 buckets would make the **load factor** 1.00, over the limit of 0.75. | c-resize-check | Hash table, 4 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.75. Bucket 1: Ann, Ben. Bucket 3: Mia. 4 ÷ 4 = 1.00 > 0.75.",
    "50 | So first, make a bigger table: 8 buckets instead of 4. | c-resize | Hash table, 8 buckets, 0 keys, load factor 0.00. Still in the old table: Ann, Ben, Mia.",
    "51 | **Rehash** Ann: with 8 buckets it belongs in bucket 5. | c-rehash | Hash table, 8 buckets, 1 keys, load factor 0.13. Bucket 5: Ann. Still in the old table: Ben, Mia. 285 mod 8 = 5.",
    "52 | **Rehash** Ben: with 8 buckets it belongs in bucket 5. | c-rehash | Hash table, 8 buckets, 2 keys, load factor 0.25. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Still in the old table: Mia. 277 mod 8 = 5.",
    "53 | **Rehash** Mia: with 8 buckets it belongs in bucket 7. | c-rehash | Hash table, 8 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.38. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Bucket 7: Mia. 279 mod 8 = 7.",
    "54 | All 3 keys moved: **O(n)**, but only now and then, so put is still **O(1)** on average. | c-resize-done | Hash table, 8 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.38. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Bucket 7: Mia.",
    "55 | Add up the letter codes of **Sid**: h("Sid") = 288. | hash-fn | Hash table, 8 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.38. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Bucket 7: Mia. h("Sid") = 288.",
    "56 | 288 mod 8 = 0, so **Sid** belongs in bucket 0. | hash-index | Hash table, 8 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.38. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Bucket 7: Mia. 288 mod 8 = 0.",
    "57 | Bucket 0 is empty, so **Sid** goes straight in. | c-put-append | Hash table, 8 buckets, 4 keys, load factor 0.50. Bucket 0: Sid. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Bucket 7: Mia.",
    "58 | Every key was **rehashed**, because its bucket depends on the table’s size. Doubling keeps that rare. | - | Hash table, 8 buckets, 4 keys, load factor 0.50. Bucket 0: Sid. Bucket 5: Ann, Ben. Bucket 7: Mia. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "59 | **Open addressing** keeps every key in the buckets themselves, one per bucket. No chains. | - | Hash table, 7 buckets, 0 keys, load factor 0.00.",
    "60 | Add up the letter codes of **Sid**: h("Sid") = 288. | hash-fn | Hash table, 7 buckets, 0 keys, load factor 0.00. h("Sid") = 288.",
    "61 | 288 mod 7 = 1, so **Sid** belongs in bucket 1. | hash-index | Hash table, 7 buckets, 0 keys, load factor 0.00. 288 mod 7 = 1.",
    "62 | Bucket 1 is empty, so **Sid** goes straight in. | p-put-place | Hash table, 7 buckets, 1 keys, load factor 0.14. Bucket 1: Sid.",
    "63 | Add up the letter codes of **Jim**: h("Jim") = 288. | hash-fn | Hash table, 7 buckets, 1 keys, load factor 0.14. Bucket 1: Sid. h("Jim") = 288.",
    "64 | 288 mod 7 = 1, so **Jim** belongs in bucket 1. | hash-index | Hash table, 7 buckets, 1 keys, load factor 0.14. Bucket 1: Sid. 288 mod 7 = 1.",
