    "67 | Add up the letter codes of **Kat**: h("Kat") = 288. | hash-fn | Hash table, 7 buckets, 2 keys, load factor 0.29. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. h("Kat") = 288.",
    "68 | 288 mod 7 = 1, so **Kat** belongs in bucket 1. | hash-index | Hash table, 7 buckets, 2 keys, load factor 0.29. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. 288 mod 7 = 1.",
    "69 | Bucket 1 holds **Sid**: a **collision**. Probe the next bucket, 2. | p-put-probe | Hash table, 7 buckets, 2 keys, load factor 0.29. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 1: collision.",
    "70 | Bucket 2 holds **Jim**. Try bucket 3. | p-put-probe | Hash table, 7 buckets, 2 keys, load factor 0.29. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 2: collision.",
    "71 | Bucket 3 is empty: **Kat** goes in here, away from its home bucket. | p-put-place | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat.",
    "72 | On a collision, **linear probing** tries the next bucket, then the next, until one is free. | - | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat.",
    "73 | Add up the letter codes of **Kat**: h("Kat") = 288. | hash-fn | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat. h("Kat") = 288.",
    "74 | 288 mod 7 = 1, so **Kat** belongs in bucket 1. | hash-index | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat. 288 mod 7 = 1.",
    "75 | Bucket 1 holds **Sid**, not **Kat**. Probe on to 2. | p-get-probe | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat.",
    "76 | Bucket 2 holds **Jim**, not **Kat**. Probe on to 3. | p-get-probe | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat.",
    "77 | Found **Kat**: 555-0101. | p-get-found | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat. Found Kat.",
    "78 | Search follows the same path, and stops at the first empty bucket. | - | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "79 | Now delete Jim. If bucket 2 were simply emptied, a search for Kat would stop there and miss it. | - | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat.",
    "80 | Add up the letter codes of **Jim**: h("Jim") = 288. | hash-fn | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat. h("Jim") = 288.",
    "81 | 288 mod 7 = 1, so **Jim** belongs in bucket 1. | hash-index | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat. 288 mod 7 = 1.",
    "82 | Bucket 1 holds **Sid**, not **Jim**. Probe on to 2. | p-remove-probe | Hash table, 7 buckets, 3 keys, load factor 0.43. Bucket 1: Sid. Bucket 2: Jim. Bucket 3: Kat.",
