  "steps": [
    "0 | A **recursive** function solves a problem by calling itself on a smaller version of it. | - | The call stack is empty.",
    "1 | It needs a **base case**, small enough to answer directly, and a **recursive case** that calls itself. | - | The call stack is empty.",
    "2 | Call **fact(1)**. 1 ≤ 1 is the **base case**: it returns 1 straight away, with no more calls. | fact-base | Call stack, top first: fact(1), base case: 1. Calls made: 1.",
    "3 | **fact(1)** = 1. Calls made: 1. Deepest stack: 1. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 1.",
    "4 | fact(1) is the base case: 1, with no more calls. Bigger n takes the recursive case. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 1. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "5 | Each call gets a **frame** on the **call stack**: its own n, and what it’s waiting for. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 1.",
    "6 | Call **fact(3)**. 3 is more than 1, so it needs **fact(2)** first: 3 × fact(2). | fact-call | Call stack, top first: fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 1.",
    "7 | Call **fact(2)**. 2 is more than 1, so it needs **fact(1)** first: 2 × fact(1). | fact-call | Call stack, top first: fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 2.",
    "8 | Call **fact(1)**. 1 ≤ 1 is the **base case**: it returns 1 straight away, with no more calls. | fact-base | Call stack, top first: fact(1), base case: 1; fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 3.",
    "9 | **fact(1)** returned 1, so fact(2) = 2 × 1 = **2**. It returns that. | fact-return | Call stack, top first: fact(2), 2 × 1 = 2; fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 3.",
    "10 | **fact(2)** returned 2, so fact(3) = 3 × 2 = **6**. It returns that. | fact-return | Call stack, top first: fact(3), 3 × 2 = 6. Calls made: 3.",
    "11 | **fact(3)** = 6. Calls made: 3. Deepest stack: 3. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 3.",
    "12 | Frames piled up on the way down and came off in reverse on the way back: last in, first out. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 3. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "13 | fact(n) = n × fact(n − 1), and fact(1) = 1. Watch fact(5). | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 3.",
    "14 | Call **fact(5)**. 5 is more than 1, so it needs **fact(4)** first: 5 × fact(4). | fact-call | Call stack, top first: fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 1.",
    "15 | Call **fact(4)**. 4 is more than 1, so it needs **fact(3)** first: 4 × fact(3). | fact-call | Call stack, top first: fact(4), 4 × fact(3); fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 2.",
    "16 | Call **fact(3)**. 3 is more than 1, so it needs **fact(2)** first: 3 × fact(2). | fact-call | Call stack, top first: fact(3), 3 × fact(2); fact(4), 4 × fact(3); fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 3.",
    "17 | Call **fact(2)**. 2 is more than 1, so it needs **fact(1)** first: 2 × fact(1). | fact-call | Call stack, top first: fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2); fact(4), 4 × fact(3); fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 4.",
    "18 | Call **fact(1)**. 1 ≤ 1 is the **base case**: it returns 1 straight away, with no more calls. | fact-base | Call stack, top first: fact(1), base case: 1; fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2); fact(4), 4 × fact(3); fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 5.",
    "19 | **fact(1)** returned 1, so fact(2) = 2 × 1 = **2**. It returns that. | fact-return | Call stack, top first: fact(2), 2 × 1 = 2; fact(3), 3 × fact(2); fact(4), 4 × fact(3); fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 5.",
    "20 | **fact(2)** returned 2, so fact(3) = 3 × 2 = **6**. It returns that. | fact-return | Call stack, top first: fact(3), 3 × 2 = 6; fact(4), 4 × fact(3); fact(5), 5 × fact(4). Calls made: 5.",
