    "78 | Solving each smaller problem only once is the heart of **dynamic programming**. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 9. Memo: f(2)=1 f(3)=2 f(4)=3 f(5)=5. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "79 | What if there’s no base case? Every call makes another, and none ever returns. | - | The call stack is empty. Calls made: 9. Memo: f(2)=1 f(3)=2 f(4)=3 f(5)=5.",
