    "85 | Call **fact(-2)**. With no base case, it always calls **fact(-3)** next, and waits. | broken-call | Call stack, top first: fact(-2), -2 × fact(-3); fact(-1), -1 × fact(-2); fact(0), 0 × fact(-1); fact(1), 1 × fact(0); fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 6.",
    "86 | Call **fact(-3)**. With no base case, it always calls **fact(-4)** next, and waits. | broken-call | Call stack, top first: fact(-3), -3 × fact(-4); fact(-2), -2 × fact(-3); fact(-1), -1 × fact(-2); fact(0), 0 × fact(-1); fact(1), 1 × fact(0); fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 7.",
    "87 | The stack is full after 7 frames, with no base case in sight. That’s a **stack overflow**. | - | Call stack, top first: fact(-3), -3 × fact(-4); fact(-2), -2 × fact(-3); fact(-1), -1 × fact(-2); fact(0), 0 × fact(-1); fact(1), 1 × fact(0); fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 7. Stack overflow.",
    "88 | Real stacks hold thousands of frames, but not endless ones. Without a base case, they always run out. | - | Call stack, top first: fact(-3), -3 × fact(-4); fact(-2), -2 × fact(-3); fact(-1), -1 × fact(-2); fact(0), 0 × fact(-1); fact(1), 1 × fact(0); fact(2), 2 × fact(1); fact(3), 3 × fact(2). Calls made: 7. Stack overflow.",
