  "steps": [
    "0 | A **linked list** is a chain of **nodes**. Each holds a value and a **next** pointer to the node after it. | - | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30.",
    "1 | Unlike an array’s slots, the nodes can sit anywhere in memory. Only the pointers keep them in order. | - | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30.",
    "2 | The last node’s next is **null**: nothing comes after it. | - | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "3 | The list itself only remembers where it starts: the **head** pointer. Lose that and you lose the list. | - | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30.",
    "4 | Many lists also keep a **tail** pointer to the last node, so they can reach the end at once. | - | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "5 | There are no indices. To visit every node, start **cur** at the head and follow **next** until it’s null. | - | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5.",
    "6 | Visit **12**. | traverse-visit | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 12.",
    "7 | Visit **7**. | traverse-visit | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 7.",
    "8 | Visit **30**. | traverse-visit | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 30.",
    "9 | Visit **5**. | traverse-visit | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 5.",
    "10 | **cur** reached null: all 4 nodes visited, from the head. That’s **O(n)**. | - | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5.",
    "11 | To reach the 4th node you must pass the first 3: getting to position i is **O(n)**, not O(1) as in an array. | - | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "12 | Make a new node for **4**. Nothing points to it yet. | head-create | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 4.",
    "13 | Point its **next** at the current head, 12. | head-link | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 4.",
    "14 | Move **head** to the new node. Nothing else moved: **O(1)**. | head-move | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5.",
    "15 | Adding at the head never touches the rest of the list, however long it is. | - | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "16 | Adding at the tail is different. This list keeps no tail pointer… | - | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5.",
    "17 | Make a new node for **9**. Nothing points to it yet. | tail-create | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9.",
    "18 | No tail pointer, so start **cur** at the head, 4, and walk. | walk | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9. cur at 4.",
    "19 | Its next isn’t null, so follow it: **cur** is at 12. | walk | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9. cur at 12.",
    "20 | Its next isn’t null, so follow it: **cur** is at 7. | walk | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9. cur at 7.",
    "21 | Its next isn’t null, so follow it: **cur** is at 30. | walk | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9. cur at 30.",
    "22 | **cur** is at 5, whose next is null: the last node. | walk | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9. cur at 5.",
    "23 | Point 5’s **next** at the new node. | tail-link | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. Being linked in or out: 9. cur at 5.",
    "24 | Done, but reaching the end took 5 steps: **O(n)** without a tail pointer. | - | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9.",
    "25 | This list keeps a **tail** pointer. Watch the difference. | - | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5.",
    "26 | Make a new node for **9**. Nothing points to it yet. | tail-create | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5. Being linked in or out: 9.",
    "27 | The **tail** pointer finds the last node, 5, at once. Point its **next** at the new node. | tail-link | Singly linked list of 5 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. Being linked in or out: 9.",
    "28 | Move **tail** to the new node. No walking: **O(1)** with a tail pointer. | tail-move | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9.",
    "29 | To insert in the middle, find the node first, then link the new one in after it. | - | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9.",
    "30 | Is **cur** (4) the **7** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. cur at 4.",
    "31 | Is **cur** (12) the **7** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. cur at 12.",
    "32 | **cur** holds **7**. Found it. | search-found | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. cur at 7. Found 7.",
    "33 | Make a new node for **21**. Nothing points to it yet. | after-create | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. Being linked in or out: 21.",
    "34 | Point the new node’s **next** at 30, the node after 7. | after-link | Singly linked list of 6 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30, 5, 9. Being linked in or out: 21.",
    "35 | Now point 7’s **next** at **21**. Pointers changed; nothing moved. | after-relink | Singly linked list of 7 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 21, 30, 5, 9.",
    "36 | Only two pointers changed, and nothing shifted as it would in an array. The cost was finding 7. | - | Singly linked list of 7 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 21, 30, 5, 9. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "37 | To delete a node, find it and the node **before** it: that node’s next is what changes. | - | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30.",
    "38 | Is **cur** (4) the **7** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | delete-find | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30. cur at 4.",
    "39 | Is **cur** (12) the **7** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | delete-find | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30. prev at 4. cur at 12.",
    "40 | **cur** holds **7**. This is the node to remove. | delete-find | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 7, 30. prev at 12. cur at 7. Found 7.",
    "41 | Point 12’s **next** past **7**, straight to 30. | unlink | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 30. Being linked in or out: 7. prev at 12.",
    "42 | Nothing points to **7** any more, so it’s gone. | - | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 30.",
    "43 | **cur** holds **4**. This is the node to remove. | delete-find | Singly linked list of 3 nodes. From the head: 4, 12, 30. cur at 4. Found 4.",
    "44 | **4** is the head: move **head** on to 12. | unlink-head | Singly linked list of 2 nodes. From the head: 12, 30. Being linked in or out: 4.",
    "45 | Nothing points to **4** any more, so it’s gone. | - | Singly linked list of 2 nodes. From the head: 12, 30.",
    "46 | Deleting the head is **O(1)**. Anywhere else, finding the node is O(n); the re-link itself is O(1). | - | Singly linked list of 2 nodes. From the head: 12, 30. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "47 | Is **cur** (12) the **30** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 12.",
    "48 | Is **cur** (7) the **30** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 7.",
    "49 | **cur** holds **30**. Found it. | search-found | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 30. Found 30.",
    "50 | Is **cur** (12) the **8** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 12.",
    "51 | Is **cur** (7) the **8** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 7.",
    "52 | Is **cur** (30) the **8** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 30.",
    "53 | Is **cur** (5) the **8** we’re looking for? No: follow **next**. | search-compare | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. cur at 5.",
    "54 | **cur** fell off the end (null): **8** isn’t in the list. That took **O(n)**. | search-not-found | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5.",
    "55 | Search checks nodes one by one: **O(n)**. A list can’t jump to its middle, so binary search can’t help. | - | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 12, 7, 30, 5. | ⏸ chapter-end",
    "56 | A classic interview question: reverse the list in place with three pointers, **prev**, **cur** and **next**. | - | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 1, 2, 3, 4.",
    "57 | Save **next** = 2, so the rest of the list isn’t lost. | reverse-save | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 1, 2, 3, 4. cur at 1. next at 2.",
    "58 | Flip 1’s **next** to **prev**, which is null: 1 will be the new tail. | reverse-flip | Singly linked list of 4 nodes. From the head: 1. cur at 1. next at 2.",
